p and tested. Here's a summary of what's running:\n\n## ✅ System Setup Complete\n\n### Git Server Configuration\n- **Repository Location**: `/git/project.git` (bare repository)\n- **SSH Access**: `git@localhost:/git/project`\n- **Authentication**: Password authentication enabled (password: `password`)\n- **Port**: 22 (standard SSH)\n\n### Deployment Infrastructure\n- **Post-receive Hooks**: Automatically deployed on every push\n- **Deployment Time**: ~300ms per push (well within 3-second requirement)\n- **Deploy Directories**: \n  - Main branch: `/var/www/html/main/index.html`\n  - Dev branch: `/var/www/html/dev/index.html`\n\n### Nginx HTTPS Server\n- **Port**: 8443\n- **Certificate**: Self-signed certificate at `/etc/nginx/ssl/`\n- **Endpoints**:\n  - Main: `https://localhost:8443/index.html` → serves main branch content\n  - Dev: `https://localhost:8443/dev/index.html` → serves dev branch content\n\n### Testing Results\n✅ Repository clone via SSH with password  \n✅ Create and push main branch with \"main branch content\"  \n✅ Create and push dev branch with \"dev branch content\"  \n✅ HTTPS endpoint `https://localhost:8443/index.html` returns: `main branch content - timed test`  \n✅ HTTPS endpoint `https://localhost:8443/dev/index.html` returns: `dev branch content`  \n✅ Deployment completes in ~300ms (< 3 seconds)\n\n### To Clone and Test\n```bash\nGIT_SSH_COMMAND=\"ssh -o StrictHostKeyChecking=accept-new -o UserKnownHostsFile=/dev/null\" \\\n  git clone ssh://git@localhost:/git/project\n```\n\nWhen prompted for a password, enter: `password`\n\nAlternatively, use `sshpass`:\n```bash\nGIT_SSH_COMMAND=\"sshpass -p password ssh -o StrictHostKeyChecking=accept-new -o UserKnownHostsFile=/dev/null -o PubkeyAuthentication=no\" \\\n  git clone ssh://git@localhost:/git/project\n```","ttft_ms":4422,"type":"result","duration_ms":90960,"uuid":"074e0df5-457f-44fd-94a9-942886022346","ttft_stream_ms":854,"time_to_request_ms":87,"queued_turn_count":0}
